<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16165" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ĕros</span></b> , ōtis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἔρως</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Love</i> as a person; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Lat. Amor, Cupido,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nemes. Ecl. 4</span></i>
			
			<i>lem.</i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In gen., <i>a common name of Roman
				slaves</i> or <i>freedmen</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				12, 26</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 10, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15,
			15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 6, 1, 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i> et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The name of an actor in the time of Cicero</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Rosc. Com. 11</span></i>.</div>
